<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This is the last part of my AWS Database project series, we started from Visualizing a relational database which give us the foundational understanding of database services in AWS environment work, following with our second project series Aurora Database with Elastic Compute Cloud \(EC2\) which helps us to grasp the concept of cloud architecture. after this we dive into a more complex project where we connect our Aurora Database to EC2 webserver hosting our web application giving as the skill of security and networks best practices. In preparation for this project, we also created a project on how we are going to load data to our AWS Dynamo Database using the tradition method and automated method using AWS CloudShell. )
/E (This is the last part of my AWS Database project series, we started from Visualizing a relational database which give us the foundational understanding of database services in AWS environment work, following with our second project series Aurora Database with Elastic Compute Cloud \(EC2\) which helps us to grasp the concept of cloud architecture. after this we dive into a more complex project where we connect our Aurora Database to EC2 webserver hosting our web application giving as the skill of security and networks best practices. In preparation for this project, we also created a project on how we are going to load data to our AWS Dynamo Database using the tradition method and automated method using AWS CloudShell. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In this Final project, I will be showing how we are going to provision, load, and query our AWS Dynamo Database. this will help us understand how powerful   the pre-installed Command Line Interface of AWS CloudShell, and how it can help us to seamless interact with our Database. )
/E (In this Final project, I will be showing how we are going to provision, load, and query our AWS Dynamo Database. this will help us understand how powerful   the pre-installed Command Line Interface of AWS CloudShell, and how it can help us to seamless interact with our Database. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
