/T (IAM is like a special account you create within your AWS account for different people or applications. It's a way to give them specific permissions to access and manage AWS resources without sharing your main account credentials. Think of it as creating separate logins for your team members, each with limited access to only what they need)
/E (IAM is like a special account you create within your AWS account for different people or applications. It's a way to give them specific permissions to access and manage AWS resources without sharing your main account credentials. Think of it as creating separate logins for your team members, each with limited access to only what they need)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
