/T (This project series documents the complete lifecycle of building, populating, and interacting with a NoSQL database using Amazon DynamoDB. Executed entirely through the AWS Command Line Interface \(CLI\), this project provided a practical, hands-on demonstration of core cloud database engineering principles, from initial design to advanced data manipulation.)
/E (This project series documents the complete lifecycle of building, populating, and interacting with a NoSQL database using Amazon DynamoDB. Executed entirely through the AWS Command Line Interface \(CLI\), this project provided a practical, hands-on demonstration of core cloud database engineering principles, from initial design to advanced data manipulation.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Next, we focused on retrieving the data. We practiced fetching specific items with get-item and querying for related records, learning that a partition key is always required. Finally, we demonstrated how to keep data in sync across multiple tables by using a single, all-or-nothing transaction command to perform a complex update.)
/E (Next, we focused on retrieving the data. We practiced fetching specific items with get-item and querying for related records, learning that a partition key is always required. Finally, we demonstrated how to keep data in sync across multiple tables by using a single, all-or-nothing transaction command to perform a complex update.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
